WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.582 --> 00:00:17.249
The beautiful ballerina gracefully stepped back from the front of the stage.

2
00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:23.934
She took one last bow as the curtain closed again and hid her from the audience.

3
00:00:25.255 --> 00:00:33.041
Immediately, the children were surrounded by a swarm of people—dancers, costumers, and stagehands.

4
00:00:34.301 --> 00:00:36.402
Everyone ignored Vinnie and Mandy.

5
00:00:36.422 --> 00:00:39.604
"Anna! Bravo!

6
00:00:39.964 --> 00:00:41.204
You were magical!"

7
00:00:41.704 --> 00:00:43.265
cried a nearby gentleman.

8
00:00:44.506 --> 00:00:47.947
He smiled at the ballerina as she walked toward him.

9
00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.128
She held an armful of roses.

10
00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:54.930
More flowers lay scattered on the stage.

11
00:00:56.650 --> 00:01:02.594
"Bring them to my dressing room," ordered the ballerina, throwing the bundle of roses to Mandy.

12
00:01:02.614 --> 00:01:06.257
"But I Mandy began.

13
00:01:07.718 --> 00:01:09.300
The dancer brushed past her.

14
00:01:11.081 --> 00:01:13.383
A man shouted at Vinnie: "You!

15
00:01:13.763 --> 00:01:15.865
Collect all of Miss Pavlova's flowers!"

16
00:01:17.526 --> 00:01:19.888
He shoved Vinnie out onto the stage.

17
00:01:22.451 --> 00:01:24.672
Someone pushed Mandy toward the dancer.

18
00:01:24.692 --> 00:01:26.874
"Hurry up!"

19
00:01:27.395 --> 00:01:28.656
the ballerina ordered.

20
00:01:29.884 --> 00:01:31.005
Mandy followed her.

21
00:01:32.566 --> 00:01:34.488
She couldn't see where Vinnie had gone.

22
00:01:36.089 --> 00:01:40.313
In the ballerina's dressing room, Mandy stood nervously by the door.

23
00:01:41.754 --> 00:01:43.815
Anna and the gentleman were arguing.

24
00:01:43.835 --> 00:01:46.918
"You are my manager, Victor!

25
00:01:46.938 --> 00:01:50.161
I wanted to dance in my other ballet shoes!"

26
00:01:51.662 --> 00:01:53.643
she cried, stamping her feet.

27
00:01:55.065 --> 00:01:56.025
"I'm sorry, Anna.

28
00:01:56.606 --> 00:02:01.093
Next time, I will bring all your shoes," Victor apologized.

29
00:02:02.594 --> 00:02:05.335
They talked loudly and with so much passion.

30
00:02:06.796 --> 00:02:08.617
Mandy watched them fascinated.

31
00:02:08.637 --> 00:02:12.079
"Where had Vinnie and I landed?"

32
00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:13.139
she wondered.

33
00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:16.741
"Girl! What are you staring at?"

34
00:02:17.302 --> 00:02:18.582
Anna was speaking to her.

35
00:02:18.602 --> 00:02:24.305
"Oh, I'm sorry, ma'am," she apologized.

36
00:02:25.706 --> 00:02:28.788
"Your flowers Mandy held them out.

37
00:02:30.368 --> 00:02:31.949
"Take them to my carriage and wait.

38
00:02:33.129 --> 00:02:34.450
You're the new girl, right?

39
00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.131
Sergei said Tatiana was sick tonight."

40
00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:43.214
Then Anna waved her arm in a way that told Mandy to leave.

41
00:02:45.655 --> 00:02:49.916
After collecting the flowers from the stage, Vinnie was given a broom.

42
00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:52.177
"Are you new here?"

43
00:02:52.738 --> 00:02:53.758
asked a young boy.

44
00:02:54.779 --> 00:02:57.780
He was about Vinnie's age and was already sweeping.

45
00:02:59.544 --> 00:03:04.188
"I guess," replied Vinnie, wondering where "here" was.

46
00:03:04.208 --> 00:03:06.370
"I'm Mikhail.

47
00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:07.771
What's your name?"

48
00:03:08.411 --> 00:03:09.172
asked the boy.

49
00:03:10.453 --> 00:03:11.874
Vinnie introduced himself.

50
00:03:13.395 --> 00:03:17.199
Both he and the boy were dressed in dark trousers and shirts.

51
00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.524
"She's a beautiful dancer," said Vinnie, starting up a conversation.

52
00:03:25.966 --> 00:03:28.648
He hoped Mikhail would reveal where they were.

53
00:03:30.112 --> 00:03:35.276
"Anna Pavlova is Russia's most famous ballerina," Mikhail said proudly.

54
00:03:35.296 --> 00:03:40.160
"She just came back from a tour of Europe and the United States."

55
00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:44.383
"Russia!" Vinnie said to himself.

56
00:03:46.045 --> 00:03:51.069
Meanwhile, Mandy was riding away in a carriage with Anna and Victor.

57
00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:55.632
As she looked back, Mandy gasped at the grand building.

58
00:03:55.652 --> 00:03:59.696
"What a gorgeous theater!"

59
00:04:00.584 --> 00:04:01.465
cried Mandy.

60
00:04:01.485 --> 00:04:07.330
"The Mariinsky Theater has brought me much success," Anna said softly.

61
00:04:08.611 --> 00:04:09.972
She seemed happier now.

62
00:04:11.473 --> 00:04:13.034
She blew the theater a kiss.

63
00:04:13.054 --> 00:04:22.282
"For your next tour," began Victor, "we will travel on the Trans-Siberian Railway to Vladivostok, and then we'll

64
00:04:22.302 --> 00:04:25.465
go Anna grew angry again.

65
00:04:25.485 --> 00:04:29.128
"What? I just got back!

66
00:04:29.532 --> 00:04:30.493
I need to rest!"

67
00:04:30.513 --> 00:04:34.376
"But, Anna," Victor said calmly.

68
00:04:34.396 --> 00:04:39.020
"Your fans all across the motherland want to see you dance!"

69
00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.903
Mandy looked out the window, amazed.

70
00:04:42.923 --> 00:04:47.627
"Vladivostok? We're in Russia!"

71
00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:48.908
she thought.

72
00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:52.791
Anna cried, "I will stay in St.

73
00:04:52.811 --> 00:04:55.954
Petersburg. I am tired, Victor!

74
00:04:56.474 --> 00:04:58.136
I will not discuss this anymore!"
